+### Compound Durations
+
+`parseCompound` sums several parts into milliseconds. Parts can be separated by spaces, commas, or nothing at all, and every part needs a unit.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms'
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m')         // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m')        // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours') // 187200000
+parseCompound('1h30m15s')       // 5415000
+```
+
+It throws a `TypeError` (with the input in the message) if the string is empty, longer than 99 characters, or any part is missing a unit or can't be parsed.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
